Basic Network Devices

A hub broadcasts information to every device on a network, similar to a radio tower.
A switch is more intelligent, making connections between specific devices and only passing data to the intended destination, which enhances security and network performance.
Connecting Networks and the Internet

A router connects multiple networks, directing information between them based on destination addresses.
A modem connects your router to the internet, bringing internet access to your local network.
Virtualization in Networking

Virtualization tools are software programs that perform the functions of physical network devices like hubs, switches, routers, and modems.
These tools offer cost savings and scalability, and are often provided by cloud service providers.
